          "metadata": {
            "stream_source": "live"
          },
          "text": "# Streaming Probe\n\n1. Always record the date and time at the start of every entry.\n2. Use objective language to describe observed behaviors without adding bias.\n3. Note the exact location where the observation is taking place.\n4. Describe the physical environment in detail to provide necessary context.\n5. Record direct quotes from participants whenever possible.\n6. Avoid using vague adjectives like \"many\" or \"few\" in favor of specific counts.\n7. Document the weather conditions if they might influence the subject's behavior.\n8. Keep a clear distinction between raw observations and personal interpretations.\n9. Use a consistent shorthand to speed up writing during active events.\n10. Note the presence of other people who may be affecting the scene.\n11. Describe the sequence of events in the order they actually occurred.\n12. Include sketches or diagrams to clarify spatial relationships.\n13. Review and expand upon shorthand notes immediately after the session.\n14. Document any interruptions or gaps in the observation period.\n15. Maintain a neutral tone to ensure the data remains scientific.\n16. Store all field notes in a secure and organized system for later analysis.",
